(j)
to prescribe the authority referred to in Sub-section (3) of Section 21 and Sub-section (2) of Section 22;
(k)
to prescribe the form and contents of the licences to be granted by an Inspector under Section 24 and the circumstances
under which they may be granted;
(l)
to prescribe scales of charges to be followed in preparing certificates under Section 27 for expenses incurred on behalf
of an owner;
(m)
to regulate the isolation, detention, treatment (including sterilization and inoculation) and disposal of animals which are
infective, or suspected of being infective and the disposal of carcasses and parts of carcasses;
(n)
to regulate the duties and powers of Inspectors;
(o)
to prescribe the manner in which any report or notice under this Act shall be made or given;
(p)
to prohibit or regulate the entry into the [State]
